  "input": "task: semantic similarity between historical scouting games\noriginal-language: pl\noriginal-title: Poznaj po ubraniu (z odmianą)\noriginal-context: Chłopiec, który ma potem poznawać, bada przedtem palcami szorstkość, grubość, sposób wykończenia i t. p. brzegu kurtek wszystkich harcerzy. Potem zawiązuje mu się oczy i podchodzą doń wszyscy pokolei, a on poznaje ich po ubraniu. *Odmiana:* poznaj po rękach, włosach, twarzy i t. d.\nparallel-language: en\nparallel-title: Identify by Clothing (with Variations)\nparallel-context: The boy who is to identify others first examines with his fingers the roughness, thickness, finishing method, and the like of the edges of all the scouts' jackets. Then his eyes are blindfolded, and each scout approaches him in turn, while he identifies them by their clothing. *Variations:* identify by hands, hair, face, and so on.",
